[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Bounded Semantic Elaboration

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEM-BIND-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Source-located instance and port binding
STATEMENT: >>>
The frontend shall derive explicit instance headers from generated syntax and bind ordered subcircuit ports using case-insensitive lexical declaration lookup. It shall retain actual/formal source syntax and named assignments, reject arity and duplicate-formal ambiguity, diagnose recursive reference graphs and duplicate instance IDs, and preserve missing, ambiguous, deferred and unsupported outcomes. Model terminal interpretation shall use explicitly supported family contracts rather than the parser's ambiguous positional partition. Binding shall neither evaluate parameters nor imply numerical device support.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: InstanceExtraction.cs, InstanceBinding.cs, DeclarationExtraction.cs and DeclarationCatalog.cs. Verification: InstanceBindingTests, including seeded order/renaming properties. The initial profile covers X/D/Q/M/J/S/W reference headers, with explicit unsupported outcomes for other terminal/model contracts. Conditional/resource-dependent references remain provisional. Recursion is checked in the observed declaration graph, including unused declarations; this is not topology flattening or full ngspice scope conformance.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SEM-CAT-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEM-PARAM-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Bounded atomic parameter elaboration
STATEMENT: >>>
Parameter evaluation shall consume generated expression syntax with explicit SPICE numeric suffixes, scope/default/override policies, finite arithmetic and dependency limits. Missing values, cycles, unsupported constructs and invalid domains shall produce source-located diagnostics without publishing partial effective values or modifying input catalogs. Syntax acceptance shall remain separate from evaluability.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: ParameterEvaluator.cs reuses generated expression contexts with catalog-branded lexical instance environments. Verification: ParameterEvaluationTests, including independent numerical tables, seeded chains/instance isolation, caller provenance, bounds and atomic dependency failures; scripts/QualifySemanticFrontend.cs compares named ngspice results. See docs/semantic-frontend.md and bounded evidence for supported semantics and unresolved qualification.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SEM-CAT-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEM-RESOURCE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Explicit bounded include and library access
STATEMENT: >>>
External resource resolution shall be opt-in with explicit permitted roots, strict declared encoding, selected library sections, cycle detection, byte/depth/file budgets and immutable source provenance. Denied paths and link traversal shall be rejected. Failed resolution shall publish no partial successful source graph. Syntax-only parsing shall never open resources, execute controls or invoke simulators.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: ResourceResolver.cs, generated resource/section metadata and explicit SourceSegment mappings. Verification: ResourceResolutionTests plus named original-versus-expanded ngspice fixtures. Link-creation testing is unavailable on the configured exFAT artifact volume and is explicitly skipped. Hostile filesystem races, Linux, conditional/complex library profiles and general ngspice preprocessing conformance remain unqualified. See docs/semantic-frontend.md and bounded verification evidence.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SEM-CAT-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEM-RESOURCE-002
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Caller-selected resource recognition limits
STATEMENT: >>>
Resource resolution shall apply the caller-selected immutable parser character/token limits to every loaded root and fragment, counting synthetic fragment prefix input against those limits. Corpus resource and expanded-source recognition shall use its explicitly selected parser profile rather than silently reverting to interactive defaults. Insufficient limits shall refuse atomically with a budget outcome; larger qualification limits shall not change the default interactive profile or bypass file, byte, depth or path policies.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: ResourcePolicy.ParsingLimits and ResourceResolver.Load, plus ResourceProfileObserver and the corpus resource_parser manifest. Verification: Explicit_parser_limits_govern_root_and_fragment_recognition, including a smaller-limit refusal and larger-limit success on both locations; full corpus replay. This is allocation-policy propagation, not a language or numerical-support expansion.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SEM-RESOURCE-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEM-RESOURCE-003
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Separate control exports from resource branch selection
STATEMENT: >>>
A csparam control-vector export alone shall not classify an otherwise unconditional include as conditional resource selection. Its syntax and deferred parameter semantics shall remain intact; resource resolution shall neither evaluate nor execute it. Actual conditional resources and other unresolved selection contexts shall remain explicitly refused under the bounded profile.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: Control_vector_exports_do_not_select_include_branches_or_gain_evaluation_support, A_control_vector_export_does_not_enable_conditional_resource_loading, and 64 seeded source-map/export cases (904,20261101). Reference: ngspice src/frontend/inp.c handles csparam control-vector creation after dotifeval. No general conditional selection, csparam evaluation or model/analysis bridge support is implied.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SEM-RESOURCE-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEM-RESOURCE-004
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Bounded physical recognition failure details
STATEMENT: >>>
A resource recognition failure shall retain at most three underlying parser diagnostics of at most 512 characters per message, associated with the failed physical source path. Included-fragment diagnostic lines shall exclude the synthetic title prefix. Failed resolution shall still publish no partial successful text or resource graph. Non-parser failures shall not invent parser diagnostics.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: ResourceDiagnostic.SyntaxDiagnostics and ResourceResolver.ParseFailure. Verification: Included_syntax_failures_retain_bounded_physical_diagnostics and retained resource-policy corpus diagnostic examples. These observations explain grammar/budget gaps; a parser rejection does not establish that a vendor file is invalid SPICE.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SEM-RESOURCE-001
